In article <1993Oct14.171856.5170@telesciences.com>, mgorman@telesciences.com (Mitch Gorman) writes:
>	Has anyone ever managed to obtain an intrinsic from a corpse when they
>	were interrupted on their first attempt to eat that corpse?  I've never
>	seen it happen.
>
>	For example, I just knocked off a black dragon.  I start eating it, but
>	some piss-ant little xan comes along and starts nibbling my boots.  I
>	take care of the xan, and go back to eating the dragon corpse.
>
>	I know, however, that I may as well not bother (unless I'm hungry), b/c
>	I will _not_ pick up the disintegration resistance from that corpse.
>
>	Is this just the way the random-number-generator falls, or is this just
>	The Way It Is?

That's just the way it is.  The bad effects (poisoning, hallucination, acid,...)
take effect with the first bite, but the chance of gaining an intrinsic is 
only checked when you finish eating.

A thought just occured to me.  Could you get a nice intrinsic without getting
aggravate monster by wishing for and then eating a "partly eaten Wizard of
Yendor corpse"? ... I just tried it and it doesn't work.  You get the
aggravate monster anyway.  Oh well.
